.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1055 AM PDT Wed Sep 23 2026

Mostly VFR currently, the exception is KHAF where LIFR conditions
persist. VFR is expected by late morning and will persist until
late this evening when sub-MVFR conditions return to the coastal
areas. There confidence is moderate for coastal locations to
receive sub- IFR and lower confidence for the Bay Area Terminals
early Thursday morning. Any low clouds or fog that does develop
will clear between 1630Z-1730Z Thursday.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Onshore winds are forecast to increase
this afternoon, yet no significant gusts expected. Wind speeds
ease overnight and into early Thursday morning with a low
confidence for sub-MVFR (10-30% probability) yet MVFR is more
likely with 20-50% probability at or around 11Z Thursday. Any low
clouds that does develop will clear between 1630Z-1730Z Thursday
with increasing onshore winds by Thursday afternoon.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Onshore winds are forecast to
increase this afternoon before easing after sunset. There is
moderate confidence to see similar conditions late this evening
and into the overnight as we saw this morning. There is moderate
confidence for sub-IFR (30-50% probability) late tonight into
Thursday morning before returning to VFR by around 17Z Thursday.

